<title>MOLDOVA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>MOLDOVA GOVERNMENT LIST (970116)</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> * 16 Jan 97 - President Petru Lucinschi asked state audit   *</p>
<p> *		 chamber head Ion Chebuk to form a new	   *</p>
<p> *		 government and said he should name his cabinet*</p>
<p> *		 within two weeks. Parliament must approve the *</p>
<p> *		 new premier within two weeks.		     *</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> President (Sworn in 15 Jan 97)................Petru LUCINSCHI</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Prime Minister-designate.........................Ion CHEBUK**</p>
<p>							  (**SEE NOTE ABOVE)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>OUTGOING GOVERNMENT (Formed 5 Apr 94, resigned 3 Dec 96)</p>
<p> Prime Minister................................Andrei SANGHELI</p>
<p>						    (Re-elected 31 Mar 94)</p>
<p> Chairman of Parliament........................Petru LUCINSCHI</p>
<p>						    (Re-elected 29 Mar 94)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p> First Deputy Prime Minister..........................Ion GUTU</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister..........................Valentin CUNEV</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister.........................Valeriu BULGARI</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister............................Grigore OJOG</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>State Minister (chief of the government staff).Gheorghe GUSAC</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture.................................Vitalie GORINCIOI</p>
<p> Communal Services &amp; Housing...................Mihai SEVEROVAN</p>
<p> Culture.......................................Mihai CIUBOTARU</p>
<p> Defence.........................................Pavel CREANGA</p>
<p> Finance........................................Valeriu CHITAN</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs...................................Mihai POPOV</p>
<p> Health Care..................................Timofei MOSNEAGA</p>
<p> Information, Computers &amp; Telecommunication.........Ion CASIAN</p>
<p> Industry.......................................Grigore TRIBOI</p>
<p> Interior....................................Constantin ANTOCI</p>
<p> Justice.........................................Vasile STURZA</p>
<p> Labour &amp; Social Protection....................Dumitru NIDELCU</p>
<p> National Economy..............................Valeriu BOBUTAC</p>
<p> National Security...............................Vasile CALMOI</p>
<p> Privatisation..................................Ceslav CIOBANU</p>
<p> Relations with Parliament.......................Victor PUSCAS</p>
<p> Science &amp; Education..............................Petru GAUGAS</p>
